meta {
  name: Get Leaderboard
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/leaderboard
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~month: 2026-08
  ~limit: 5
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns the office total and a ranked list", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.month).to.match(/^\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])$/);
    expect(body).to.have.property("officeTotalPremium");
    expect(body.entries).to.be.an("array");
  });

  // THE PRIVACY CONTRACT. This is why a producer is allowed to read the whole
  // agency here at all — see the docs below. If this test ever fails, the
  // endpoint has started leaking colleagues' numbers.
  test("no entry exposes another producer's dollars", function () {
    for (const entry of res.getBody().entries) {
      expect(entry).to.not.have.property("premium");
      expect(entry).to.not.have.property("goalPremium");
    }
  });

  test("the caller's own row carries their own figures", function () {
    const self = res.getBody().self;
    if (self !== null) {
      expect(self).to.have.property("premium");
      expect(self).to.have.property("goalPremium");
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /leaderboard — Motivation Hub (PAC-13)

  Office total, ranked standings, and the caller's own progress.

  - **Module:** `leaderboard` (must be enabled for the agency)
  - **Permission:** `leaderboard:read`
  - **Read-only** — `PATCH /leaderboard` is a `404`.

  ## ⚠ Deliberate `DataScope` bypass

  This endpoint reads **agency-wide regardless of the caller's data scope**. A
  producer whose scope is `own` still sees the office total and every
  colleague's rank — that is the entire product requirement, not an oversight,
  and it is the one endpoint in the API that does not apply the scope clamp.

  What that buys is bounded by the **response contract** instead:

  - `entries[]` carry `rank`, `name`, `initials` and `attainmentPct` —
    a position and a ratio. **Never a dollar figure.**
  - `officeTotalPremium` is the only aggregate dollar figure.
  - `self` carries dollars, because that is the caller's own data.

  Do not add `premium` to an entry, and do not "fix" the missing scope clamp.
  Both are asserted above and in the API e2e suite.

  Branch is likewise ignored — "office" means the agency. A per-branch
  leaderboard has no product definition yet.

  ## Month-scoped, not range-scoped
  There is **no `range` param**, and the dashboard's time chips deliberately do
  not drive this card. `producerGoals` stores one goal per producer per month,
  so a "% to goal" for a week would mean prorating a monthly target — a decision
  nobody has made, and a fabricated number on a motivation panel is worse than
  no number. The card is labelled *Monthly Goal* for that reason.

  ## Query params
  | param | type | default | rules |
  |-------|------|---------|-------|
  | month | string | current Chicago month | `YYYY-MM` |
  | limit | int | 5 | 1–25. The caller's own row may be appended **beyond** it |

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "month": "2026-08",
    "officeTotalPremium": 46071,
    "producerCount": 5,
    "self": {
      "producerId": "6a70...156",
      "rank": 1,
      "premium": 31662,
      "goalPremium": 60000,
      "attainmentPct": 52.8,
      "isOutsideTop": false
    },
    "entries": [
      { "producerId": "6a70...156", "name": "Pat Producer", "initials": "PP",
        "rank": 1, "attainmentPct": 52.8, "isSelf": true }
    ]
  }
  ```

  ## Ranking
  By **`attainmentPct` descending**, not by premium. Attainment is the only
  quantity rendered per row, so a list ordered by a number the viewer cannot see
  reads as broken. Producers with no goal sort last, ordered among themselves by
  premium. Ties share a rank and the next rank skips.

  Two rules worth knowing:
  - Producers with a goal but **no sales** are included — a board that shrinks
    in a slow month is the opposite of motivating.
  - The caller's row is **always** present, appended at its true rank with
    `isOutsideTop: true` when it falls outside `limit`.

  `attainmentPct` is `null` when the producer has no goal row for the month, or
  the goal is `0`. The UI renders an em dash, never `0%`.

  ## Errors
  - `400` — malformed `month` (e.g. `2026-5`, `2026-13`), or `limit` outside 1–25.
  - `401` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403` — `leaderboard` module disabled, or missing `leaderboard:read`.

  > **Deploy note:** PAC-13 grants Branch Manager `leaderboard:read`. Existing
  > agencies only pick that up after `npm run sync:roles:dev -w @sfa/api`, and
  > signed-in clients keep their cached permissions until the next refresh.
}
